  "narrative": {
    "intro": "KBR Wyle Services has $531M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. KBR Wyle Services won 132 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $4M. KBR Wyle Services obligations are down 17.0% year over year. KBR Wyle Services has grown since FY21, when obligations were $278M, and peaked in FY25 at $640M before the current-year decline to $531M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buying agency at $339M, followed by Department of the Interior at $71.5M and Department of Defense at $53.8M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market at $147M, with Engineering Services at $131M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $67.9M. This picture shows a company concentrated in R&D and engineering markets with one dominant customer, and a fiscal-year-to-date total that reflects a noticeable year-over-year reduction in obligations.",
